<p>(a)  Includes $8,403 restructuring charge.</p>
<p>(b)  Operating income is net of $1,040 of severance costs incurred.</p>
<p>(c)  Includes charge of $24,595 related to the recapitalization of Quanterra.</p>
<p>(d)  Other income includes the gain on the settlement of the Motco litigation net of costs related to certain incineration equipment specially constructed for the Motco project which has been idle since ceasing work on the project, and legal and other expenses.</p>
<p>(e)  Includes $7,500 tax credit resulting from the adjustment of IT's deferred tax asset valuation allowance and $9,970 tax benefit related to the loss on recapitalization of Quanterra.</p>
<p>(f)  Net income (loss) per common share is computed by dividing net income (loss) applicable to common stock by the weighted average number of common and common equivalent shares outstanding.  For all periods above, net income (loss) per common share, computed based upon the assumption that all of the Company's convertible exchangeable  preferred stock is converted into common shares, is antidilutive and therefore not presented.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
